cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "Forecasting the Future"
abstract: >-
  Probability forecasts for ten binary US macroeconomic questions at horizons from one month to
  ten years, from a two-chain hidden Markov model over economic regimes blended with a
  persistence chain, evaluated walk-forward on point-in-time data under pre-registered rules.
authors:
